    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Fibonacci Spiral" DecimalsToShow="2" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="57.5" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13: each Fibonacci number is the sum of the two before it. Squares with these sides fit together into a rectangle - every new square is exactly as wide as the two before it side by side.\n\nA quarter circle in each square, corner to corner, makes a spiral. Every quarter turn it grows by about the same factor, close to 1.618, the golden ratio. A snail shell grows by a steady factor too, which is why it looks alike.\n\nCount the spirals of seeds on a sunflower head or of scales on a pinecone: you get two neighbors from this list.\n\nDrag the yellow points to turn and resize it." DecimalsToShow="2" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="105.5" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
